[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
# Authoring requirements

Requirements define externally observable behavior, constraints, edge
conditions, error handling, and explicitly identified safety behavior.

They should not prescribe architecture, source layout, libraries, algorithms,
or tasks unless a mandated safety or compliance control requires a particular
solution.

Use immutable UIDs with this form:

```text
REQ-[MODULE]-[TYPE]-[NNN]
```

Supported type segments are:

- `US` for user stories
- `FR` for functional requirements
- `EC` for edge-case requirements
- `ERR` for error-handling requirements
- `SAFE` for safety requirements.

Copy the records below and assign new UIDs. Do not reuse the template UIDs for
project requirements.

A good requirement is necessary, unambiguous, feasible, singular enough to
verify, implementation-independent where possible, traceable, and supported by
objective acceptance criteria.

Use `shall` for normative behavior. Define actors, modes, quantities, units,
tolerances, timing, preconditions, fault conditions, and expected failure
behavior whenever they affect acceptance.

Safety requirements must trace to a risk control or safety function and define
the applicable modes, safe state, timing, fault reaction, reset behavior, and
objective evidence as applicable.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TEMPLATE-US-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template user story
TYPE: REQUIREMENT
CATEGORY: UserStory
PRIORITY: Medium
SAFETY_CLASS: NotSafetyRelated
STATEMENT: As a defined user role, I want a stated capability so that I receive a measurable benefit.
RATIONALE: Explain why the user needs the capability and why the benefit matters.
ACCEPTANCE: Given the relevant context, when the user performs the action, then the expected result is observable.
TAGS: template, user-story

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TEMPLATE-FR-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template functional requirement
TYPE: REQUIREMENT
CATEGORY: Functional
PRIORITY: High
SAFETY_CLASS: NotSafetyRelated
STATEMENT: The system shall provide the defined observable behavior under the specified operating conditions.
RATIONALE: Explain why the behavior is required.
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Given:
- the system is in the specified initial state
- required inputs and dependencies are available.
When:
- the defined action or event occurs.
Then:
- the measurable expected result is produced
- prohibited side effects do not occur.
<<<
