[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TEMPLATE-SAFE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template safety requirement
TYPE: REQUIREMENT
CATEGORY: Safety
PRIORITY: Critical
SAFETY_CLASS: SafetyCritical
OPERATING_MODES: Autonomous and remote operation
SAFE_STATE: Hazardous motion is commanded to the validated safe state and automatic restart is inhibited
RESPONSE_TIME: Replace with the derived maximum response time, including units and tolerance
INTEGRITY_TARGET: Replace with the target derived using the approved risk and functional-safety method
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test, fault injection, analysis, and representative validation
STATEMENT: When the defined hazardous condition or safety-function demand occurs in an applicable operating mode, the system shall achieve the defined safe state within the allocated response time.
RATIONALE: This requirement implements the template protective-stop risk control and safety function.
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Given:
- the applicable operating mode and worst-case permitted load
- the specified environmental and surface conditions
- relevant single faults and justified fault combinations
- the release-candidate hardware, software, parameters, and calibration.
When:
- the defined safety demand is introduced.
Then:
- detection, logic, communication, actuation, and stopping remain within their allocations
- the defined safe state is reached within the required response time
- diagnostics identify the demand and detected faults
- restart remains inhibited until the defined reset conditions are satisfied.
Evidence:
- retained raw results
- approved test and analysis reports
- configuration and calibration identification
- independent review where required.
<<<
