[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
# External work-management mapping

Synchronization fields are optional. Omit them when no configured adapter owns
a Git-managed representation.

A direct mapping consists of `SYNC_ADAPTER` and `EXTERNAL_ENTITY_ID`. Related
entities use one deterministic role-qualified entry per line:

```text
implementation: external-entity-id
verification: external-entity-id
```

The local StrictDoc UID remains authoritative. Do not infer mappings from
titles or statements, and never store credentials in project documents.

# Review checklist

Before activating a requirement, confirm that:

- all template wording has been replaced
- the UID is unique and immutable
- the statement has one clear normative interpretation
- acceptance criteria produce an objective pass or fail result
- units, timing, tolerances, modes, and limits are explicit
- edge and error behavior are separated when independently verifiable
- parent relations resolve to the intended records
- safety requirements trace to risk controls or safety functions
- synchronization mappings are explicit, deterministic, and credential-free.
<<<
